{number: 113}
{title: A Shelter in the Time of Storm}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
The [C] Lord's our Rock, in Him we hide,
A Shelter in the time of [G7] storm;
Secure whatever ill betide,
A [C] Shelter in the [G7] time of [C] storm.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Oh, [F] Jesus is a Rock in a [C] weary land,
A weary land, a [G7] weary land;
Oh, [F] Jesus is a Rock in a [C] weary land,
A [C] Shelter in the [G7] time of [C] storm.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
A [C] shade by day, defense by night,
A Shelter in the time of [G7] storm;
No fears alarm, no foes affright,
A [C] Shelter in the [G7] time of [C] storm.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
The [C] raging storms may round us beat,
A Shelter in the time of [G7] storm;
We'll never leave our safe retreat,
A [C] Shelter in the [G7] time of [C] storm.
{end_of_verse}
